# Every line here describes behaviour Plan 1 already implements and verified
# by other means. If the runner disagrees with any of it, the runner is wrong.

# The guest resolves the gateway.
0.000 < arp who-has 192.168.127.1 tell 192.168.127.2
0.000 > arp reply 192.168.127.1 is-at 5a:94:ef:e4:0c:ee

# The guest pings the gateway; the payload comes back verbatim.
0.010 < icmp echo_request id 4660 seq 42
0.010 > icmp echo_reply id 4660 seq 42

# Nothing is listening on port 53, so the gateway refuses.
0.020 < udp 4000 > 53 (12)
0.020 > icmp unreachable port
